## 5. Notes for review

- **No `api.js` edit.** `modules/apiLogs.js` is instantiated with the shared `API` instance inside `useApiMonitoring.js`, exactly like `useInfra.js` consumes `API.infra`. If you later wire the module into `initializeAPI()`, the view keeps working unchanged.
- **Server-side history, no client buffer.** Unlike `useInfraMonitor.js` (Docker only exposes snapshots), API metrics are already aggregated by the backend, so no sample array exists — the chart plots the returned buckets only.
- **Live is off by default** (30 s when enabled) — a monitoring screen must not flood the very API it is measuring. The interval selector stays visible but disabled while paused.
- **Path filter never empties:** `state.endpointOptions` is refreshed only when no path filter is set, so the selector keeps every endpoint instead of collapsing to the filtered one.
- **Admin scope:** the "All users" toggle is gated on `$storex.users.isAdmin` and switches every request to `/api/api-logs/admin/*`; the `username` / `project` filters are only sent in that mode (user-scoped routes already filter by the authenticated user).
- **Registration path:** menu → `$storex.$navigation.openApp('api-monitoring')` → `config/apps.js` → panel (desktop) or route `/:projectName/api-monitoring` (single/mobile) → `AppRouteView` → `APP_COMPONENTS_MAP['api-monitoring']`.
- **Accessibility:** every control has an associated label or `sr-only` label, preset buttons expose `aria-pressed`, tables use `scope="col"` headers, and all interactive rows are real `<button>`s.

