## 4. Why this matches your symptom

- **"Only after resizing the container"** → `chart.update('none')` never re-measures. `hasSizeChanged()` + `chart.resize()` now performs that re-measure automatically; the chart is also created one tick later so it is born with the real panel size.
- **"Nothing at all changes"** → a single failing aggregation used to discard the whole round (`Promise.all`), and a hung request used to block every future refresh forever (`inFlight`). Both paths now keep the dashboard updating; a broken endpoint only degrades its own card and stays visible in the banner instead of silently freezing the view.
- `state.revision` gives the canvas an explicit "numbers changed" edge, independent of payload identity.

## 5. Accessibility / UX check (unchanged but verified)

- Error banner keeps a real message (not colour-only) and a keyboard-reachable `Dismiss`.
- New `revision` prop is purely programmatic, no interactive target added.
- Focus rings, `aria-pressed` on the range presets and `sr-only` labels untouched.

## 6. What to verify

1. Leave **Live** on for ~2 min: the "last updated" clock, KPI strip, tables and the graph must all move together.
2. Break one endpoint (`/api/api-logs/errors` → 500): the other cards must still refresh, with the banner naming the failure.
3. Open the panel while it is not the active tab, then switch to it: the graph must already be drawn (no resize needed).

