## 4. Anti-Patterns Avoided

- ❌ Treating `resize()` as a data repaint — it re-measures, it does not re-parse.
- ❌ Comparing measured pixels exactly when one side is fractional (`round1` vs `clientWidth`).
- ❌ `deep: true` on a computed that already returns a fresh object graph (O(buckets) walk per poll).
- ❌ Leaving a hovered overlay showing pre-refresh numbers.

## 5. Validation Checklist

- [ ] Change the grouping (`10s` → `minute`): axis labels switch bucket width immediately, then the refetched series replaces them.
- [ ] Press **Refresh** / enable **Live**: every poll repaints (verify with the bucket counter next to the title).
- [ ] Apply an endpoint/status/duration filter: the curve shrinks to the filtered set.
- [ ] Resize the dockview panel: the graph re-fits **and keeps updating** afterwards (regression guard for defect 1+2).
- [ ] Hover, then let a refresh land: the overlay disappears instead of showing stale values.
- [ ] Leave the panel hidden in another tab, come back: it repaints with the latest payload.

