Looking at the two files, I found the root cause of the "not refreshing" behaviour and the reason the values disappear on hover.

## Diagnosis

**1. The chart instance is stored in reactive state**

`data()` is wrapped by Vue with a deep proxy. `this.chart = new Chart(...)` therefore returns (on every read) a **proxy** around the Chart.js instance. Chart.js keeps identity-sensitive internals (`_metasets`, controllers, `WeakMap` keys, `_animations`). Calling `proxy.update('none')` mixes raw and proxied objects — `update()` runs but the canvas keeps the previous frame. This is the classic Vue 3 + Chart.js pitfall and it matches exactly "changes the data, nothing repaints".

**2. The tooltip is delegated to a hand-rolled overlay that never renders**

`plugins.tooltip.enabled: false` + a custom `external` handler + a `v-if` overlay. That path is fragile (model shape, `opacity`, positioning inside a resizable dockview panel). The user sees no values at all. The reliable way is Chart.js' own tooltip, drawn on the canvas, configured to the dark palette (values of *all four* series on `mode: 'index'`).

## Change summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/views/api-monitoring/ApiMonitoringChart.vue` | Store the instance with `markRaw()` so it is never proxied; patch datasets **in place** (same dataset objects, new `data` arrays) then `chart.update('none')`; rebuild only when the option signature changes; replace the custom overlay with Chart.js' native tooltip (index mode, dark palette, per-axis units); drop the now-unused overlay state/handlers. |

